<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain GRASS

  create_player_lands
  {
    terrain_type GRASS
    land_percent 10
  }

<TERRAIN_GENERATION>

/* 70 create_terrain SNOW { base_terrain GRASS land_percent 100 } */

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>


/*
================================================================================
RMSTEST_82c - control for 82a. The same comment, opened by the literal number
70 instead of a word.
Feeds: docs/token-alias-design.md Sec.3.1 and slice B.

The header is at the bottom on purpose and names no constant whose number is
a comment marker or a control word.

PREDICTION, written 2026-11-02 before the run. GRASS everywhere. RMSTEST_57
showed the literal 69 does not open a comment, only a word valued 69 does, so
the literal 70 should not close one either. SNOW here would mean literals do
count for 70, and the lexer rule in slice B would have to cover them.
Read: probe_scenario.py, terrain histogram.

Generate at: Tiny, 2 players, seed 1000, scenario editor.
================================================================================
*/
